   1248  f7f4							; ========================================================================
   1249  f7f4							; SetObjectXPos — Andrew Davie algorithm (page-aligned table)
   1250  f7f4							; X=0 positions P0, X=1 positions P1
   1251  f7f4							; A = pixel position (0-159)
   1252  f7f4							; ========================================================================
   1253  f7f4				   SetObjectXPos_b1
   1254  f7f4		       85 02		      sta	WSYNC
   1255  f7f6		       38		      sec
   1256  f7f7				   .Div15Loop
   1257  f7f7		       e9 0f		      sbc	#15
   1258  f7f9		       b0 fc		      bcs	.Div15Loop
   1259  f7fb		       a8		      tay
   1260  f7fc		       b9 0f fe 	      lda	fineAdjustTable_b1,Y
   1261  f7ff		       95 20		      sta	HMP0,X
   1262  f801		       95 10		      sta	RESP0,X
   1263  f803		       60		      rts
   1264  f804
   1265  f804							; Bar H3c tables (B=0..120): content ≤71c (WSYNC 3c fits in 76).
   1266  f804							; Paths (cycles after WSYNC → sty red): F=0 slim 12+5A; F=1 slim+nop 14+5A;
   1267  f804							; F=2 full 20+5A; F=3 full 30+5A; F=4 full 31+5A (A=0 special-cased).
   1268  f804							; D2 (2026-10-16): both tables were EXACTLY period-8 ([1-8],[9-16],…) so
   1269  f804							; they shrank 121→15 entries, indexed (B+7)>>3 (see the reader). Entry 0 =
   1270  f804							; B=0; entry g≥1 = B in [8(g-1)+1, 8g]. Verified against the old 121B blobs.
   1271  f804				   BarDelayTable		; (B+7)>>3, 15 entries
   1272  f804		       00 02 03 02*	      .byte.b	0, 2,3,2,4,5,2,5,7,8,5,8,10,11,8
   1273  f813				   BarFineTable 		; (B+7)>>3, 15 entries; ∈{0,1,2,3,4}
   1274  f813		       02 01 00 02*	      .byte.b	2, 1,0,2,1,0,4,2,1,0,4,2,1,0,4
   1275  f822
   1276  f822							; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   1277  f822
   1278  f822							; ==============================================================================
   1279  f822							; Raft (enemy type 7) — the moving, rideable platform. plans/raft_moving_plan.md
   1280  f822							; ==============================================================================
   1281  f822							; Entrance: bank0 UEDispatch -> CallPad_RaftBody (sta $1FF7 / jmp $F822) -> here;
   1282  f822							; exit: jmp ReturnPad ($FBF8, bank1's twin) -> bank0's jmp UE_Next.
   1283  f822							; CallPad rules honoured: no nested CallPad, no bank0 jsr, ZP is shared RAM.
   1284  f822							; ZP ALIAS WARNING: this code uses bank0's Temp at $88 (free here — every other
   1285  f822							; overscan Temp consumer, the joystick read and the hot-bump flag, ran before
   1286  f822							; UpdateEnemies). It must NEVER touch bank1's Temp symbol ($AD = bank0's
   1287  f822							; TickCounter — writing that would stall the game timer).
   1288  f822							;
   1289  f822							; User spec 2026-10-18: floats only on water; carries the player across and
   1290  f822							; returns; ~1.5x the player's 1 px/frame; inertia when it starts.
   1291  f822							;   Y	     = a FIXED line (RAFTER_Y), not the authored y: the water surface is
   1292  f822							;	       the same in every water room (the band's last 12 lines), so the
   1293  f822							;	       raft always looks like it is floating, and the rider's RoomY
   1294  f822							;	       (RAFTER_Y-12 = 118) stays 7 px clear of the 125 water-kill line.
   1295  f822							;	       This write lands after RefreshEnemyY, so the VBL draws it.
   1296  f822							;   Speed   = 1 px on even frames, 2 px on odd (EnemyRamP parity) = 1.5 px/frame.
   1297  f822							;   Inertia = the raft holds the frame on which it turns around (it does not
   1298  f822							;	       move that frame). A true multi-frame spin-up ramp would need one
   1299  f822							;	       byte of per-raft state and the ZP map has none free (EnemyRamD's
   1300  f822							;	       high nibble is bank1's RoomDarkMask — verified, not free), so the
   1301  f822							;	       ramp is a deliberate simplification; ask and I carve a byte.
   1302  f822							;   Range   = derived from the playfield, no data and no ZP: the model row-2
   1303  f822							;	       cell just beyond the raft's leading edge is read from the PF row-2
   1304  f822							;	       buffers and a SOLID cell turns it around, so the raft patrols
   1305  f822							;	       exactly the open water span of the room.
   1306  f822							;   Ride    = while the player's box overlaps the raft's upper rows and he is not
   1307  f822							;	       rising (vyHi >= 0): pin RoomY to the raft's top, zero vy (gravity
   1308  f822							;	       must never accumulate into the water) and carry RoomX by the
   1309  f822							;	       raft's own step. Thrust up (vyHi < 0) skips the pin, so the player
   1310  f822							;	       can always fly off.
   1311  f822							; In: X = enemy slot. Clobbers A/Y and bank0 Temp ($88).
   1312  f822							; ==============================================================================
   1313  f822							; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   1314  f822							; CallPad_RaftBody twin — BYTE-IDENTICAL with kernel.asm's copy at $F8C0 (guard:
   1315  f822							; verify_build.check_raft_tramp). bank0 executes `sta $1FF7` at $F8C0-$F8C2 and
   1316  f822							; the fetch at $F8C3 comes from THIS bank: `jmp $FDE3` = RaftBody below. Neither
   1317  f822							; bank runs the other's half — bank0's operand bytes are never fetched, bank1's
   1318  f822							; `sta $1FF7` is never executed (it is only the swapped-out image's prefix).
   1319  f822							; In bank1's $F822-$F936 fill, so the $F937 pin does not move.
   1320  f822							; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   1321  f822		       00 00 00 00*	      .ds	$F8C0 - *, 0
   1322  f8c0		       8d f7 1f 	      .byte.b	$8D, $F7, $1F	; sta $1FF7 (twin)
   1323  f8c3		       4c e3 fd 	      .byte.b	$4C, $E3, $FD	; jmp $FDE3 (twin — fetched post-switch)
   1324  f8c6
   1325  f8c6		       00 00 00 00*	      .ds	$F937 - *, 0	; pinned: bank2 M1StripBlast back-jmp operand
   1326  f937							; ($F937) — test_bomb_strip asserts both literals
   1327  f937							; StripBlastCheck — Phase 4: bomb blast vs the D6 patch strips. Tail-jumped
   1328  f937							; from BombMarkWalls .BMWDone, which now crosses to bank2 FIRST (M1 twin,
   1329  f937							; `sta $1FF8 / jmp $F970` — the meta lives in bank2's ROM) and comes back
   1330  f937							; here (`sta $1FF7 / jmp $F937`). Still 0 pushes (the jsr+pha version
   1331  f937							; measured SP $F7 < the $F8 gameplay guard, and the pha leaked on the
   1332  f937							; early-exit path -> runaway work -> 309-line frames in Stella 2026-10-04).
   1333  f937							; Every exit ends in ReturnPad with A = count.
   1334  f937							; In: BMWScratch = strip left col pL in RIGHT-half space ($FF = none/sym,
   1335  f937							; captured before the punch loop), CollisionEndX/CellX = blast window in
   1336  f937							; LEFT-half space (bomb col mirrored at BMW entry), CollisionX = count.
   1337  f937							; Overlap after mirroring (39-x) with the strip not yet dead → set
   1338  f937							; EnemyDeadMask b3 (ball strip; b4 = M1 strip, set by M1StripBlast) and
   1339  f937							; inc the count (caller's +75 loop scores it). The
   1340  f937							; kill bits die with the room (EnterRoom zeroes EnemyDeadMask) — same
   1341  f937							; lifecycle as WallMask holes (D1-B). P2b door models never
   1342  f937							; reach .SBtake: M1StripBlast (bank2, runs first) stashes BMWScratch :=
   1343  f937							; $FF when MetaB b7 — the take's window test then falls into .SBdone.
   1344  f937							; Key pickup (P5) sets b3/b4 for doors instead (key-only unlock).
   1345  f937							; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   1346  f937				   StripBlastCheck
   1347  f937							; --- P2b left strip take (staged by bank2 M1StripBlast) --------------
   1348  f937							; RectCount = 2ℓ left dcol, $FF = none / left door / right bomb.
   1349  f937							; Window is still LEFT-half here (the mirror below). Door models stage
   1350  f937							; $FF both ways (MetaA b3 / MetaB b7) so neither take runs — key (P5)
   1351  f937							; sets b3/b4 instead.
   1352  f937		       a5 92		      lda	RectCount
   1353  f939		       30 1e		      bmi	.SBright	; $FF → no left strip this frame
   1354  f93b		       a5 8c		      lda	CollisionCellX	; blast hi
